  "editorialSummary": "Nothing says peak modernity quite like the FAA recovering from a [nationwide ground stop](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/why-a-problem-on-the-ground-can-affect-flights-thousands-of-miles-away-among-other-issues) while Nvidia [recoils from an executive scandal](https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/14/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-board.html) and Tesla [pivots to personal robotaxis](https://oglobo.globo.com/economia/tecnologia/noticia/2026/11/14/tesla-convida-clientes-para-comprar-robotaxi-para-uso-pessoal.ghtml). At this rate, the researchers mapping [the brain's basal ganglia](https://english.elpais.com/science-tech/2026-11-12/scientists-create-largest-ever-map-of-brain-region-tied-to-parkinsons-alzheimers-schizophrenia-and-autism.html) are likely just searching for an escape hatch.",
